Helios vkd3d-proton fork: ECL fence made ahead for the next batch

Conduit, D3D12 on NVK, Nvk12EclSync=2. Applied after 0008.

Each ExecuteCommandLists made its RM fence (ecl_fence_create, a
SEMSURF_FENCE_CREATE escape: a host round trip) between the commit and the
HE12 v4 Render whose admission releases the batch, so every batch's
admission waited for it.

- helios_vkd3d_prepare_ecl_fence(queue): reserve the queue's next ECL value
  and make its fence now (the UMD calls it right after an ECL was admitted,
  still serialised with that queue's ECLs). The next commit takes the pair
  instead of reserving and creating inline; a value whose fence was refused
  is still taken (it is next in order) and that batch makes its fence
  inline. A prepared fence left at queue destruction is closed.
- helios_vkd3d_ecl_fence_stats appends fences made ahead and taken.

